/-- The subset `𝔏₀(k, n)` of `ℭ(k, n)`, given in (5.1.10).
Not to be confused with `𝔏₀(k, n, j)` which is called `𝔏₀'` in Lean. -/
def 𝔏₀ (k n : ℕ) : Set (𝔓 X) :=
  { p ∈ ℭ k n | 𝔅 k n p = ∅ }

